| Eval metrics log       | `trading-brains.tft_predictions.retraining_eval_logs` (with `symbol` column) |


## Supported Tickers

| Ticker | Name            | Model checkpoint                        | Status   |
|--------|-----------------|-----------------------------------------|----------|
| SPY    | S&P 500 ETF     | `tft_checkpoint_SPY_latest.ckpt`        | Active   |
| GOOG   | Alphabet Inc.   | `tft_checkpoint_GOOG_latest.ckpt`       | Active   |
| QQQ    | Nasdaq-100 ETF  | `tft_checkpoint_QQQ_latest.ckpt`        | Training |
| TSLA   | Tesla Inc.      | `tft_checkpoint_TSLA_latest.ckpt`       | Training |
| AAPL   | Apple Inc.      | `tft_checkpoint_AAPL_latest.ckpt`       | Training |

### Adding a New Ticker

Replace `AAPL` below with the desired Polygon.io ticker symbol.

**Step 1 — Train the model** (Vertex AI, ~12 hours):

    gcloud ai custom-jobs create ^
    --region=europe-west6 ^
    --project=trading-brains ^
    --display-name=tft-retrain-AAPL ^
    --worker-pool-spec=machine-type=n1-standard-8,replica-count=1,container-image-uri=gcr.io/trading-brains/tft-training ^
    --args="--polygon_api_key=IYHqABfrpYN6yfa7bFS9LLNxwJzpn0YE,--gcs_bucket=tft-for-trading-brains,--symbol=AAPL,--max_epochs=25,--lookback_days=425"

This fetches 1-min data from Polygon, trains a TFT, uploads the checkpoint to
`gs://tft-for-trading-brains/tft_checkpoint_AAPL_latest.ckpt`, and logs
evaluation metrics to the `retraining_eval_logs` BigQuery table.

**Step 2 — Verify the model works** (after training job completes):

    curl "https://tft-predictions-137489665103.europe-west6.run.app/test?ticker=AAPL"

**Step 3 — Create Cloud Scheduler jobs** for automated hourly predictions:

    gcloud scheduler jobs create http tft-hourly-prediction-aapl ^
    --location=europe-west6 ^
    --project=trading-brains ^
    --uri="https://tft-predictions-137489665103.europe-west6.run.app/predict?ticker=AAPL" ^
    --http-method=POST ^
    --schedule="0 10-16 * * 1-5" ^
    --time-zone=America/New_York ^
    --attempt-deadline=180s

    gcloud scheduler jobs create http tft-record-actuals-aapl ^
    --location=europe-west6 ^
    --project=trading-brains ^
    --uri="https://tft-predictions-137489665103.europe-west6.run.app/record_actuals?ticker=AAPL" ^
    --http-method=POST ^
    --schedule="5 11-17 * * 1-5" ^
    --time-zone=America/New_York ^
    --attempt-deadline=180s

**Step 4 — Update this readme**: add the new ticker to the Supported Tickers
table above and to the Cloud Scheduler Jobs table in the API Endpoints section.

No code changes or container rebuilds are needed — the serving container
automatically loads the correct per-ticker model from GCS on first request.


## Model Details

- **Framework**: pytorch-forecasting 1.6.1 `TemporalFusionTransformer`
- **Target**: `close` (1-min close price, per-ticker model)
- **Prediction horizon**: 60 minutes ahead (quantile predictions at 15/30/45/60 min)
- **Encoder length**: 60 time steps
- **Normalizer**: `GroupNormalizer(groups=["group"], transformation="softplus")`
- **Loss**: `QuantileLoss()` (7 quantiles)
- **Hyperparameters**: hidden_size=32, attention_head_size=2, dropout=0.1, lr=0.001, hidden_continuous_size=16, output_size=7
- **Features**: 76 engineered features (returns, SMA, MACD, volatility, ATR, Bollinger bands, RSI, stochastic, ROC, volume indicators, OBV/VPT/MFI, VWAP ratios, time features, volume lags)


