## Retraining the Model

### 1. Rebuild the training container (only if train.py or features.py changed)
gcloud builds submit --tag gcr.io/trading-brains/tft-training --project trading-brains c:\Users\batzi\OneDrive\Dokumente\trading_brains\pipeline

### 2. Submit a retraining job on Vertex AI
### Retrain SPY
gcloud ai custom-jobs create ^
--region=europe-west6 ^
--project=trading-brains ^
--display-name=tft-retrain-SPY ^
--worker-pool-spec=machine-type=n1-standard-8,replica-count=1,container-image-uri=gcr.io/trading-brains/tft-training ^
--args="--polygon_api_key=IYHqABfrpYN6yfa7bFS9LLNxwJzpn0YE,--gcs_bucket=tft-for-trading-brains,--symbol=SPY,--max_epochs=25,--lookback_days=425"

### Example: Retrain GOOG with extended batch sizes, more neurons and high memory machine
gcloud ai custom-jobs create ^
--region=europe-west6 ^
--project=trading-brains ^
--display-name=tft-retrain-GOOG ^
--worker-pool-spec=machine-type=n1-highmem-16,replica-count=1,container-image-uri=gcr.io/trading-brains/tft-training ^
--args="--polygon_api_key=IYHqABfrpYN6yfa7bFS9LLNxwJzpn0YE,--gcs_bucket=tft-for-trading-brains,--symbol=GOOG,--max_epochs=15,--lookback_days=450,--batch_size=128,--hidden_size=64,--attention_head_size=4"

The `--symbol` flag determines which ticker to fetch from Polygon and where to store
the model (`tft_checkpoint_{SYMBOL}_latest.ckpt`). Cloud Run loads the per-ticker model
on first request and caches it in memory.

### Training arguments

| Argument              | Default | Description                     |
|-----------------------|---------|---------------------------------|
| `--polygon_api_key`   | required| Polygon.io API key              |
| `--gcs_bucket`        | tft-for-trading-brains | GCS bucket for model |
| `--gcs_model_path`    | tft_checkpoint_{symbol}_latest.ckpt | GCS path (auto-set per ticker) |
| `--symbol`            | SPY     | Ticker symbol                   |
| `--lookback_days`     | 420     | Days of historical data         |
| `--max_epochs`        | 10      | Maximum training epochs         |
| `--batch_size`        | 64      | Training batch size             |
| `--learning_rate`     | 0.001   | Learning rate                   |
| `--hidden_size`       | 32      | TFT hidden size                 |
| `--attention_head_size`| 2      | Number of attention heads       |
| `--dropout`           | 0.1     | Dropout rate                    |
| `--patience`          | 10      | Early stopping patience         |

### Monitor the job

Check status in the Vertex AI Custom Jobs console:
https://console.cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/training/custom-jobs?project=trading-brains

Or via CLI:
gcloud ai custom-jobs list --region=europe-west6 --project=trading-brains --limit=5

### Start the cloud run services to log prediction data to Big Query
##### Service to populate tft_predictions_logs for US-Market hours
gcloud scheduler jobs create http tft-hourly-prediction-goog ^
  --location=europe-west6 --project=trading-brains ^
  --uri="https://tft-predictions-137489665103.europe-west6.run.app/predict?ticker=GOOG" ^
  --http-method=POST --schedule="0 10-16 * * 1-5" ^
  --time-zone=America/New_York --attempt-deadline=180s

##### Service to populate tft_actuals
gcloud scheduler jobs create http tft-record-actuals-btc ^
  --location=europe-west6 --project=trading-brains ^
  --uri="https://tft-predictions-137489665103.europe-west6.run.app/record_actuals?ticker=BTC" ^
  --http-method=POST --schedule="5 11-17 * * 1-5" ^
  --time-zone=America/New_York --attempt-deadline=180s


## Deploying the Serving Container

After changes to `main.py`:

gcloud builds submit --tag gcr.io/trading-brains/tft-predictions --project trading-brains c:\Users\batzi\OneDrive\Dokumente\trading_brains

gcloud run deploy tft-predictions --image gcr.io/trading-brains/tft-predictions --region europe-west6 --project trading-brains


## Data Sources

- **Training**: Polygon.io REST API — 1-min OHLCV bars (free tier returns "DELAYED" status, which is fine for historical data)
- **Inference**: Twelve Data API — 1-min OHLCV bars (real-time for predictions)


## Building a Trading Architecture in Alpaca

Cloud Scheduler (*/15 min)
       │
       ▼
Cloud Run "tft-trader" service
       │
       ├── 1. Call /predict endpoint (or query BQ) → get signal
       ├── 2. Apply strategy logic (entry/exit/sizing)
       ├── 3. Place orders via Alpaca API
       └── 4. Log trades to BigQuery

See 'Architecture.md' inside the directory 'trading' for very detailed documentation